id: pm-slack-fitn
title: Read Slack digests through the complete SDK corpus and refuse unreadable records
description: The fixed digest directory list omits configured item types such as Chore and its scalar parser silently skips malformed or unreadable records. Replace the package-owned parser with the public listAllComplete SDK operation. Supersedes the implementation approach in pm-slack-06ti while preserving formatting and aggregation semantics.
type: Issue
status: blocked
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-29T17:22:22.309Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T10:27:23.667Z"
author: codex-slack-digest-0929
acceptance_criteria: Configured custom item directories and escaped titles appear in digests; Unreadable or malformed source records fail before any webhook request; Complete SDK reads include terminal items and refuse truncation or omissions; Real installed CLI and packed Node/Bun acceptance preserve dry-run and digest behavior; All mandatory source coverage and documentation gates and exact-head reviews pass before merge
risk: medium
blocked_reason: "Digest code was delivered by PR 120, but acceptance still awaits blocked pm-slack-5fb5: complete-source coverage including scripts, an independent statement metric, full internal documentation, and substantive exact-head reviews. No acceptance exception is asserted."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-slack-5fb5,blocked_by,"2026-09-29T17:31:30.144Z",codex-slack-digest-0929,local,asserted
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-02T18:39:49.636Z",pi-land,"Greptile 4136613100 (setup failure skips cleanup) is valid: reproduced empirically on the pre-fix pattern (a rejected createExtensionTestHarness left one pm-slack temp directory in tmpdir). Fix: corpus tests now use a createCorpusFixture helper that registers the full teardown hook (harness deactivate, server close, directory removal) on the owning TestContext immediately after mkdtempSync, before any risky setup; added a regression pair asserting the directory is removed when later setup never runs. Release:check 265/265, zero skips."
  "2026-10-02T18:39:52.626Z",pi-land,"Greptile 4136613100-adjacent P1 4136613086 (standalone extension may not load) is refused: pm's installer links every installed package copy to the exact running host CLI (node_modules/@unbrained/pm-cli symlink, linkHostedPmCliDependency in pm-cli install-sources; EXTENSIONS.md: 'Runtime modules use static SDK imports; installed copies receive a host SDK link'), and pm-slack declared the peer dependency since its initial commit, so the listAllComplete import resolves for npm, GitHub, bundled, and local sources; the PR body records real npm/Node/Bun packed-install activation. The stale comment claiming '@unbrained/pm-cli is not resolvable at runtime' contradicted the import ten lines below it; corrected it to state the host-link contract and raw-entry precondition (docs EXTENSIONS.md standalone entries need the host SDK link before runtime SDK imports)."
  "2026-10-02T21:05:21.573Z",pi-grok,"Cubic 4168801843 is valid: a rejected deactivate skipped server close and rmSync. releaseCorpusResources now attempts deactivate, server close, and directory removal independently and rethrows the first failure. Regression tests fail on the old sequence and pass after the fix."
  "2026-10-02T21:05:22.297Z",pi-grok,"Cubic 4168801878 is valid: the slack digest block comment still said the command reads the pm store directly. It now says the complete tracker is read through the public SDK listAllComplete() operation. A source assertion locks that wording."
  "2026-10-02T21:05:22.925Z",pi-grok,"Cubic 4168801872 is refused. Pinned SDK 2026.9.29 listAllComplete throws PmCliError with a numeric exitCode for corrupt documents (list_source_incomplete, exit 1), missing roots (exit 3), and non-directory roots (exit 2). runCommandHandler rethrows that class, so the dynamic-command wrapper does not fall through and the digest is not read twice. Wrapping it in CommandError would hide those SDK exit codes behind generic exit 1. The malformed-corpus test now asserts the rejection carries a numeric exitCode."
  "2026-10-02T21:05:23.583Z",pi-grok,Cubic 4168801861 is valid. status in_progress contradicted blocked_reason and the open blocked_by edge to pm-slack-5fb5. Restoring status blocked. This PR still must not merge until that complete-source quality blocker and final-head review receipts clear.
  "2026-10-02T21:41:11.281Z",codex-sol,"Restart audit: previous 393bcb9 is pushed. New CodeRabbit 4169899823 teardown masking finding is valid; add a failing regression, preserve first failure, rerun locked full gate. No merge or item closure."
  "2026-10-02T21:44:25.161Z",codex-sol,"CodeRabbit 4169899823 fixed test-first: null-byte path makes real rmSync throw, preserving deactivate error identity despite subsequent close/removal failures; removal-only error still propagates. Focused and PM-linked suite 11/11; flock-protected npm ci and release:check pass, 270/270 tests, measured 100% lines/branches/functions. All-source/statements/docstring prerequisite pm-slack-5fb5 and pending reviews remain open."
  "2026-10-21T18:45:30.826Z",codex-agent,"Authorized tracker reconciliation, audit 2026-10-21. Owner-authorized takeover of any historical assignment for this verified terminal transition. Reverified current main f4dce1dcf2b2: merged #120 (b58f8bb); source tree exactly matches the audited snapshot. **Read Slack digests through the complete SDK corpus and refuse unreadable records.** [PR #120](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/pull/120) (b58f8bb) replaces digest reads with certified complete SDK reads; real unreadable/custom-type fixtures refuse before webhook delivery."
  "2026-10-22T10:23:39.880Z",codex-agent,"PR 146 review continuation: both unresolved findings are valid; latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Current main f4dce1dcf2b291a99d6c9e3f99fb529b104c707f contains the delivered digest implementation but still omits scripts and independent statement coverage. The unchanged acceptance criteria and blocked_by pm-slack-5fb5 prohibit recording full acceptance. Reusing this existing item for the corrections, preserving its criteria, blocker edge and all historical records. The duplicate statement-metric closure will get truthful changelog input rather than an implementation claim."
  "2026-10-22T10:24:22.284Z",codex-agent,"PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM6vDvm_ corrected through a new transition: restored blocked status, retained the original acceptance criteria and blocked_by pm-slack-5fb5, and cleared terminal acceptance fields. Historical closure entries remain unchanged. Self-review of all 10 reconciled items found the other eight delivered records have narrower delivery evidence: OIDC/main-ref/preflight guards and protected-PR publish ordering, the canonical attestation launcher, failing-realpath docstring guard, SHA-pinned workflow adoption, and dated certification merge ancestry. No other item claims the unmet full-source/independent-statement acceptance. Product source, dependencies and thresholds match main exactly."
  "2026-10-22T10:27:20.756Z",codex-agent,"Final PR 146 evidence: all 10 original reconciliation records rechecked against main f4dce1dcf2b291a99d6c9e3f99fb529b104c707f. Both unresolved findings are valid and corrected; no outside-diff findings. npm ci passed (0 vulnerabilities); npm run changelog:full and npm run changelog:check passed; pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers passed all 10 checks in a clean clone with isolated HOME, with one historical provenance advisory. pm test pm-slack-fitn --run --only-last --progress passed the selected tracker evidence command (1/1): restored blocked status, exact retained criteria/dependencies, cleared terminal acceptance fields, retained duplicate relationship, truthful generated notes, append-only history and unchanged product source. Evidence against original snapshot e4242a9 fails closed versus required blocked; tracker-only work needs no production-code behavioral revert. Existing linked-run persistence is disabled by policy. Source, dependency pins, dist and coverage thresholds remain unchanged. No history rewriting, new closures, thread replies/resolutions, merge or release. Claim released for orchestrator verification; this item remains blocked by pm-slack-5fb5."
notes[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T17:28:18.672Z",codex-slack-digest-0929,"TDD: real SDK Maintenance fixture was omitted (0 vs 1) and malformed isolated TOON did not reject before the change. Both pass after replacing the package-owned scalar parser and fixed folder list with listAllComplete({}, {pmRoot,noExtensions:true}). Public SDK init/create/close signatures verified from installed declarations. Existing digest fixtures now use initialized SDK trackers. Published dependency pins CLI and pm-ops 2026.9.29, pm-changelog 2026.9.25, with reproducible lockfile and published launcher byte identity."
  "2026-09-29T17:33:57.585Z",codex-slack-digest-0929,"Packed nine-file allowlist passed public-safe content inspection. SHA256 02c6c3da3178a80a19a088345442af311987c257c3c435aeef9b7aa55a23a6fe. Clean npm/Node and Bun installs exercised real package activation, custom-type digest (total 1), unchanged item history, and corrupt-source refusal. Measured one-item wall time Node 493ms and Bun 1198ms. Direct release gate passed 263/263 tests, zero skips, 100% lines/branches/functions for index.ts only. Docstring gate: 7 files and 51 selected declarations. Independent statements and operational-script coverage are unmeasured. pm-slack-5fb5 blocks release. ESLint/jscpd are absent from the direct dependency set; Trivy/ShellCheck unavailable on PATH. Strict health passed with preexisting stale/provenance advisories, while validate reports metadata/resolution/files/command-reference debt."
  "2026-09-29T17:34:28.290Z",codex-slack-digest-0929,"Fixture correction: SDK-created trackers now pass both cwd and pmRoot explicitly, so a linked-test sandbox cannot redirect fixture initialization. The first PM-linked full run exposed a cwd-only helper and is retained as failed evidence rather than treated as an upstream defect. Multi-item acceptance measures 12 items and 13 bucket updates, not unlimited corpus size or concurrent-writer snapshot consistency."
  "2026-09-29T17:37:00.074Z",codex-slack-digest-0929,"PM-linked full release:check now passes 263/263, zero skips and zero failure categories in tracker/source mode after giving the SDK fixture helper an explicit pmRoot. Earlier 180-second timeout is preserved in the test ledger. This was package-test context configuration, so no upstream issue was filed. Final direct release:check also passes. Generated dist is required by the existing Git-install contract and verified by CI rebuild drift checks."
  "2026-09-29T17:39:09.971Z",codex-slack-digest-0929,"Candidate PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/pull/120. Initial tested commit https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/commit/ee477c634b8e5091bc8309166a21de6dd3e6ec9f. Available exact-head CI and configured Greptile/CodeRabbit review are requested for the final linked checkpoint. Sourcery already reports a skipped review; this is missing review, not approval. Candidate is not merged, published or deployed."
  "2026-09-29T17:46:48.122Z",codex-slack-digest-0929,"CodeRabbit review 5356292908 at 7f4f8224fb096e82c6ec406edce86629ce608d01 posted one valid finding: test helper trackers survived after the suite. Comment 4136542354 received a positive reaction. The helper now accepts TestContext, registers recursive removal of its own mkdtemp directory before SDK init, and all 13 callers pass the owning test context. Full release:check remains 263/263 with zero skips. Both passing setup and setup/assertion failures run lifecycle cleanup. The next pushed head requires a fresh reviewer receipt; the earlier review is not final-head approval."
